// =====================================================================================
// D2 - Risky workload identity detected (High or Medium)
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Maps to  : POC Test A - Admin Confirms SP Compromised (and the end-state of C and D)
// Table    : AADServicePrincipalRiskEvents   (diagnostic category: ServicePrincipalRiskEvents)
// Severity : 1 (Error)
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What it finds
//   Every High or Medium risk detection Entra ID Protection has raised against a
//   service principal, excluding ones already remediated or dismissed.
//
// Detection types you will see here
//   adminConfirmedServicePrincipalCompromised  Manual  - SOC asserted compromise
//   leakedCredentials                          Auto    - Microsoft Threat Intelligence
//   suspiciousSignIns                          Auto    - ML: unusual IP / impossible travel
//   anomalousServicePrincipalActivity          Auto    - ML: deviation from baseline
//   maliciousApplication                       Auto    - Threat intel app match
//
// Why it matters
//   This is the exact signal the Conditional Access "service principal risk" condition
//   evaluates. If a row appears here and the CA policy is enforced, that identity is
//   already being denied tokens. Low is deliberately excluded to avoid false positives
//   on minor behavioural noise.
//
// Triage
//   1. Read RiskEventType first - it tells you whether a human or the ML engine decided.
//   2. adminConfirmed* means someone already investigated. Find their ticket.
//   3. Automatic detections need corroboration: check D1, D3, and D4 for the same AppId.
// =====================================================================================

let Lookback = 7d;
AADServicePrincipalRiskEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(Lookback)
| where RiskLevel in ("high", "medium")
| where RiskState !in ("remediated", "dismissed")
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    ServicePrincipalDisplayName,
    ServicePrincipalId,
    AppId,
    RiskEventType,
    RiskLevel,
    RiskState,
    RiskDetail,
    DetectionTimingType,
    Activity,
    IpAddress
| order by TimeGenerated desc
